./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-vault-remember-unlock-r1-gemini.out:4:- **Fail-Soft Error Handling on IDB Write in `unlockVault`**: §4.3 does not specify exception handling for `idb.put()` failures (e.g. Private Browsing mode blocking IDB, `SecurityError`, or storage quota exceeded). If `idb.put()` rejects or throws, `unlockVault` MUST NOT crash or block the master password unlock flow. It must catch the IDB error gracefully, log a warning, degrade to memory-only unlock (`rememberUnlock = false`), and succeed.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-vault-remember-unlock-r1-gemini.out:8:- **Explicit Key Usages Assertion**: Explicitly verify during `importKey` and after IDB retrieval that `cryptoKey.usages` includes both `"encrypt"` and `"decrypt"`. A key restored without `"encrypt"` usage will cause subsequent secret additions/edits (`persistSession`) to throw `InvalidAccessError`.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-vault-remember-unlock-r1-gemini.out:9:- **Transient `keyBytes` Zeroization**: In §4.3 Step 4, immediately after `crypto.subtle.importKey` completes, zero-fill the temporary PBKDF2 derived `keyBytes` buffer (`keyBytes.fill(0)`) if the session is operating in `CryptoKey`-only mode.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-vault-remember-unlock-r1-gemini.out:13:Using WebCrypto `extractable: false` `CryptoKey` persisted in IndexedDB prevents attackers from exporting raw key bytes for off-site offline decryption. However, because IndexedDB is origin-bound and accessible to all scripts on that origin, an XSS attacker can execute on-device decryption via `crypto.subtle.decrypt` using the handle from IndexedDB at any time.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-profile-vault-codex-r4.out:15:R4 re-review vault plan after R3 fold: VaultSnap absent/present identity, persistent meta.gen tombstone for clearVault ABA, migration.entries exact value receipt before legacy delete, iter capped before PBKDF2. VERDICT MUST_FIX NITS ALL_CLEAR only. Plan: docs/plans/2026-07-22-profile-secrets-vault.md
